From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bas=20Magr=C3=A9?= <bas@opvolger.net>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:07:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] PCI: dwc: Export dw_handle_msi_irq()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Glue drivers that share the MSI interrupt line with other interrupt
sources (e.g. SpacemiT K1, where INTx arrives on the same line) need to
call dw_handle_msi_irq() from their own chained handler.  Export it so
that works when the glue driver is built as a module.

Signed-off-by: Bas Magré <bas@opvolger.net>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
index 06722259d2e3..e18c944be01e 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware-host.c
@@ -85,6 +85,7 @@ void dw_handle_msi_irq(struct dw_pcie_rp *pp)
 			generic_handle_demux_domain_irq(pp->irq_domain, irq_off + pos);
 	}
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(dw_handle_msi_irq);
 
 /* Chained MSI interrupt service routine */
 static void dw_chained_msi_isr(struct irq_desc *desc)
